# What goes into the VSIX — an allow-list, not a deny-list.
#
# Everything is excluded, and each line below re-admits one thing the extension executes or the
# Marketplace displays. The previous form was the other way round, naming things to leave out,
# and it failed the way deny-lists fail: it carefully excluded `.git/`, `node_modules/` and
# `src/` — none of which vsce would have packaged anyway, since they cannot be reached from this
# directory — while saying nothing about `coverage/`, which is generated right here and shipped
# 34 files and 667 KB of HTML renderings of our own source whenever someone had run the coverage
# task before packaging.
#
# The cost of this direction is real and worth stating: a new runtime asset is invisible until
# somebody adds it here, and the symptom is a feature that silently does not work rather than a
# fat download. That trade is deliberate — see jpipe-vscode ADR-VSC-0020 — and it is why
# `scripts/check-vsix.sh` compares the packaged result against `vsix-contents.txt` on every
# build, in both directions.
#
# vsce always includes package.json and generates the manifest, so neither is listed.

**

# The bundles. This is the extension: two CJS entry points and the webview's assets, all
# self-contained esbuild output with no node_modules behind them.
#
# Admitted by extension rather than as `!out/**`, because vsce applies every negation *last*
# rather than letting later lines win: `!out/**` followed by `out/**/*.map` does not re-exclude
# the source maps, it ships them, and the VSIX more than doubles to 1.9 MB. Naming the kinds we
# run leaves the `.map` files out by construction instead of by a rule vsce will not honour.
!out/**/*.cjs
!out/**/*.js
!out/**/*.css

# Grammar and editor behaviour for `.jd` files.
!syntaxes/**
!language-configuration.json

# The published contract for the compiler's diagnostic report. Not loaded at runtime, but it is
# what `src/shared/diagnostic-report.ts` declares itself to mirror, and anyone reading it out of
# an installed extension is doing something reasonable.
!schema/**

# The extension icon, the two command icons the preview toolbar uses, and the one image the
# shipped README renders. `images/mcscert.svg` is deliberately absent: 95 KB that nothing —
# manifest, README or source — refers to.
!images/logo.png
!images/icon_dark.svg
!images/icon_light.svg
!images/mcscert.png

# What the Marketplace shows on the extension's page.
!README.md
!LICENSE
